---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data.mjs";
import { orderTerms } from "../../ordering.mjs";
import BubbleSampleCheckMap from "../../components/BubbleSampleCheckMap.astro";
import GarmentSampleCheckMap from "../../components/GarmentSampleCheckMap.astro";
const path = "/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/";
const title = "How to Approve Mailer and Garment Bag Samples";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, publisher: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, dateModified: "2026-11-08", inLanguage: "en" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guides", item: `${site.origin}/guides/` }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Sample approval", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
const records = [
  ["Sample identity", "Date, sample type, product model and revision"],
  ["Dimensions", "Outer size, usable inner space, units and agreed tolerances"],
  ["Appearance", "Finish reference, artwork version, print sides and color reference"],
  ["Packing", "Actual contents, packing steps, checks and observations"],
  ["Label trial", "Label stock and dimensions, placement, filled sample reference, adhesion and scan observations"],
  ["Shipping measurements", "Original bag dimensions, filled parcel dimensions and weight, units and intended carrier/service"],
  ["Changes", "Each correction, its owner and how it will be confirmed"],
  ["Approval", "Named approver, approval date and retained reference sample"]
];
---
<Layout title="Mailer & Garment Bag Sample Approval Checklist | Welltroy" description="Check poly and bubble mailers and frosted or clear garment slider bags. Review fit, closure, artwork and labels; download a garment sample approval record." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]}>
  <section class="page-hero approval-guide-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/">Buying Guides</a> / Sample approval</div><p class="eyebrow">Before bulk production</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">Approve a mailer or garment inner-bag sample against the specification you intend to order. Check the fit with your actual packed product, review the artwork on the chosen material, and record corrections before confirming the approved version.</p><p class="muted">By Welltroy · Updated <time datetime="2026-11-08">8 November 2026</time></p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#sample-type">Sample types</a><a href="#fit">Mailer fit &amp; closure</a><a href="#garment-sample-trial">Garment slider bags</a><a href="#artwork">Artwork</a><a href="#shipping-label-trial">Label trial</a><a href="#bubble-sample-trial">Bubble sample checks</a><a href="#record">Approval record</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main">
    <p>This guide covers poly and bubble shipping mailers and garment zipper inner bags. Start with the relevant <a href="#fit">shipping-mailer fit checks</a>, <a href="#garment-sample-trial">frosted / clear garment slider-bag checks</a> or <a href="#bubble-sample-trial">bubble-mailer checks</a>. Review the actual construction and packed contents; a digital artwork proof does not establish physical fit or closure performance.</p>
    <h2 id="sample-type">What Can an Existing Sample, Digital Proof or Custom Sample Confirm?</h2>
    <p>A stock sample, artwork proof and custom printed sample answer different questions. Ask which details your sample represents and which still need confirmation for the production order.</p>
    <p class="table-scroll-hint">Scroll the table to compare what each reference can establish.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Existing sample, digital proof and custom sample comparison"><table><caption>Confirm which reference represents each part of your proposed order</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Reference</th><th scope="col">Useful checks</th><th scope="col">Still to confirm</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Existing product sample</th><td>Its actual material, construction and closure; an initial packing trial.</td><td>Which size, surface, artwork and process differ from your order.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Digital artwork proof</th><td>Wording, artwork version, orientation, placement and reserved label area.</td><td>Physical fit, surface effect, print appearance, adhesion and closure.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Custom physical sample</th><td>The agreed configuration and checks it actually represents.</td><td>Any difference from bulk material, printing or construction, plus unresolved corrections.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Agree the available sample route first. A request for a custom sample does not mean the sample has already been made or approved.</p>
    <h2>Start with a Written Sample Brief</h2>
    <p>Record the packaging type and role, model or requested size, dimensions and units, material specification, finish, closure, print sides and quantity per design. Include your destination and the product that will go inside. Confirm the sample route before dispatch.</p>
    <p>Choose the format you plan to buy: <a href="/products/poly-mailers/">Poly Mailers</a>, <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/">Poly Bubble Mailers</a>, <a href="/products/metallic-bubble-mailers/">Metallic Bubble Mailers</a> or <a href="/products/zipper-bags/">Garment Zipper Bags</a>. If the format is still open, start with the <a href="/guides/choose-a-mailer/">mailer selection guide</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="fit">How Do I Check That My Product Fits a Poly or Bubble Mailer?</h2>
    <ol><li>Pack the product with its retail box, inserts, tissue or other components.</li><li>Measure usable inner space separately from catalogue outer dimensions. The bubble lining, seams and packed thickness affect fit.</li><li>Insert the contents, close the flap without forcing it, and check where the shipping label will go.</li><li>Photograph the sealed pack and record measurements. If several products will share one mailer, check each intended pack.</li></ol>
    <p>Use the <a href="/guides/mailer-size-for-clothing/">clothing mailer size guide</a> for a garment measurement workflow. A nominal outer size alone does not establish that a packed item fits.</p>
    <h2 id="garment-sample-trial">How Should I Check a Frosted or Clear Garment Slider Bag Sample?</h2>
    <p><strong>Use the actual folded garment, inserts and intended label to check usable space, loading, full zipper reclosure and appearance.</strong> Record the sample and specification versions first. Welltroy mainly supplies frosted garment bags, with clear bags also available and slider zippers as the primary closure; approve the offered material, finish and closure together.</p>
    <GarmentSampleCheckMap />
    <dl class="garment-sample-checks">
      <div><dt>1. Identify what the sample represents</dt><dd>Record the offered material, size convention, finish, closure and artwork revision. Note differences between an existing sample and your proposed bulk order. A digital proof can check artwork details, while physical fit and slider operation need the relevant physical sample.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>2. Try the real fold and usable opening</dt><dd>Measure the folded width, length and greatest thickness with tags and inserts. Check usable space between seams and below the zipper, then load and remove each intended garment group or set. Record strain, interference or excess movement. Catalogue outer dimensions alone do not confirm fit.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>3. Review slider travel and full reclosure</dt><dd>Use the opening and reclosure method agreed for the sample. Check for snagging, an incompletely closed section, seam strain or inserts pressing into the closure. Agree the check conditions and acceptance criteria; this checklist does not prescribe a universal cycle count or strength rating.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>4. Check finish, logo and identification</dt><dd>Compare the physical frosted or clear reference with the garment inside. Review logo placement, orientation and label visibility. If barcode reading is part of your workflow, trial the intended label and scanner and record the result. A finish name alone does not establish opacity or readability.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>5. Test the inner and outer layers together</dt><dd>Measure the closed inner pack again, select the intended outer mailer and try each complete customer-order combination. Check loading and outer sealing. Keep inner garment labels separate from the outer courier-label trial; a zipper inner bag alone is not a confirmed outer shipping construction.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <h3>Record the Decision and Any Recheck</h3>
    <p>For each relevant check, keep the observation or photo reference and mark <strong>accepted for this stated check</strong>, <strong>change required</strong> or <strong>not checked / pending</strong>. Give each open item an owner and a recheck reference. Keep untested features open before written production approval, and repeat affected checks when the garment fold, inserts, material, size, zipper or artwork changes.</p>
    <p>If warning text, hole positions or a particular material document is needed, record the exact request and who will confirm it. Use the <a href="/materials-and-documents/?product=zipper-bags#document-request-builder">product-specific document request</a> to clarify available evidence and scope.</p>
    <div class="guide-callout garment-record-download" id="garment-sample-record"><h3>Keep One Garment Bag Sample Record per Version</h3><p>Use the blank record for the sample reference, check observations, corrections, outer-pack mapping and dated written decision. Attach the completed TXT record to your enquiry if you need a specification review, subject to the form's current file limits.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/downloads/garment-bag-sample-approval.txt" download>Download Garment Sample Record (TXT)</a><a class="text-link" href="/quote/?product=zipper-bags#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Discuss a Garment Bag Sample →</a></div></div>
    <p>For finish selection and garment-to-bag mapping, see the <a href="/guides/apparel-inner-bags-and-shipping-mailers/#sku-record">clothing inner-bag and outer-mailer guide</a>. Sample availability, preparation and courier charges are confirmed through the <a href="/ordering/#samples">sample route</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="artwork">How Do I Check Logo Printing on a Mailer Sample?</h2>
    <p>Check the logo version, wording, print sides, placement and orientation against the approved file. Agree how color will be assessed and which physical reference will be retained. Use the <a href="/guides/logo-artwork-checklist/">logo artwork checklist</a> to prepare your files.</p>
    <p>For poly mailers, Welltroy mainly uses screen printing; the printing route is selected according to the buyer's artwork and requirements. Confirm the offered process for your specification. For a metallic mailer, identify the exact finish: metallic and holographic are different descriptions, so request confirmation of the available surface.</p>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>See a real customization case:</strong> the <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#bubble-mailer-cases">LUMIÈRE bubble mailer case</a> shows a branded packaging example. Use it as a visual reference; your sample and approved specification must describe your own order.</div>
    <h2 id="shipping-label-trial">Will the Shipping Label Work on My Finished Mailer?</h2>
    <p>Reserve space using your actual label dimensions before approving the artwork. For metallic or holographic mailers, include the selected surface reference in the trial; label compatibility needs its own check.</p>
    <ol><li><strong>Identify the trial:</strong> record the bag/sample revision, label stock, label dimensions, artwork and intended contents. Agree the application and handling checks with your packing team.</li><li><strong>Apply and close:</strong> load the complete pack, close the flap and apply the intended label in the agreed area. Check for lifting, wrinkles or interference with the opening.</li><li><strong>Read and record:</strong> inspect the label and try the intended scanner after the agreed handling check. Save photographs, observations and changes with the sample reference; recheck affected details after a specification change.</li></ol>
    <p>For US shipments, <a href="https://www.usps.com/ship/packages.htm" rel="noopener">USPS label-placement guidance</a> keeps labels on one side without overlap or bending around edges. Use your carrier's current instructions for the selected service. A successful sample trial does not establish carrier approval for every shipment.</p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/downloads/mailer-label-and-sample-check.txt" download>Download a blank label and sample check record (.txt) ↓</a> Add the completed record or reference photos to your enquiry when you need a specification review.</p>
    <h2 id="bubble-sample-trial">What Should I Check Before Approving a Bubble Mailer Sample?</h2>
    <p><strong>Use the proposed bag, your complete contents and the intended shipping label.</strong> Record which parts of the sample represent the bulk order before checking fit, lining, closure, artwork and label performance.</p>
    <BubbleSampleCheckMap />
    <p>For dimensions and finish selection, use the <a href="/guides/kraft-vs-poly-bubble-mailers/#usable-size">bubble mailer inner/outer size illustrations</a> and <a href="/guides/metallic-vs-holographic-bubble-mailers/#match-a-reference">existing-bag reference checklist</a>. Keep any box, insert or extra protective layer in the trial so a change in packing does not go unnoticed.</p>
    <h3>Record What the Sample Represents</h3>
    <p>Identify the sample, material, usable size, liner, closure, artwork and surface version. If an existing sample has a different color, size or print process, record that difference rather than treating it as approval of the missing feature. Ask which details need a further proof or physical sample.</p>
    <h3>Keep a Decision for Each Check</h3>
    <ul><li><strong>Accepted for the stated check:</strong> record the observation, method and retained sample reference.</li><li><strong>Change required:</strong> describe the correction, who will confirm it and which check will be repeated.</li><li><strong>Not checked / pending:</strong> identify what is still needed and keep that item open before production approval.</li></ul>
    <p>A fit check and an artwork check answer different questions. Agree any complete-pack handling or transit assessment with the relevant packing or quality team. Do not infer impact protection, water resistance or carrier approval from a photograph, an intact liner or a successful insertion trial.</p>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Before written approval</strong><p>Resolve the open items, identify the approved specification and artwork versions, retain the agreed sample and confirm that the quotation describes the same configuration. Recheck affected details if the size, film, liner, closure, surface or artwork changes.</p></div>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/downloads/mailer-label-and-sample-check.txt" download>Download the Sample Check Record</a><a class="text-link" href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#brief-specification-checks">Request Poly Bubble Sample Details →</a></div>
    <h2 id="record">Keep an Approval Record</h2>
    <p>Use the following fields as an approval checklist. Fill them with your actual sample information.</p>
    <p class="table-scroll-hint">On a small screen, swipe the table to read both columns.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Custom mailer sample approval record"><table><caption class="sr-only">Fields to record before approving a custom mailer sample</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What to record</th></tr></thead><tbody>{records.map(([item, detail]) => <tr><th scope="row">{item}</th><td>{detail}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <p>If you change size, material, artwork or closure after approval, ask which checks need repeating. Keep the final written specification with the approved reference and <a href="/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/">matching quotation</a>.</p>
    <h2>Request Your Sample Route</h2>
    <p>{orderTerms.design} Poly mailers, bubble mailers and garment zipper bags have a minimum order of 500 pieces; confirm the quantity breakdown by product, size, color and artwork in your quote. {orderTerms.sample}</p>
    <p>See <a href="/ordering/#samples">sample choices and ordering terms</a> before planning your launch. Send your product, quantity, packed dimensions and destination, and tell us which parts of the sample you need to evaluate.</p><a class="button" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request a sample proposal</a>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Your next step</p><h2>Keep the Order Consistent</h2><div class="guide-options"><a href="/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/"><strong>Compare quotations</strong><span>Match the price to the approved specification</span></a><a href="/guides/logo-artwork-checklist/"><strong>Prepare artwork</strong><span>Check files, placement and print sides</span></a><a href="/ordering/"><strong>Plan the order</strong><span>Samples, payment and delivery milestones</span></a></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/">All buying guides →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
